# One local per landscape (docs/STORY.md §8), through the real keys: each stands
# at the village of their own land nearest where he woke, and the one `use` key
# opens their own words. A big world, because a small one is a single island
# that may not have been dealt these lands at all.
#
#   tools/tour.sh tours/locals.tour --seed=7 --size=1024 --hour=11 --weather=clear:0
#
# `at cast:NAME` asks 49_cast where that person stands, never a coordinate.
#
# **THIS COVERS THREE OF SEVENTEEN, AND THE COUNT IS HERE SO IT CANNOT HIDE.**
# `StoryPlan.SPINE` holds seventeen local slots; pell, mica and brannoc below are
# the only ones any tour in this repository walks up to. The other fourteen are
# held by `tests/story/test_locals.gd` (every inhabited landscape has exactly one,
# each standing in their own land) and by `test_arcs.gd` (every line fits the
# glass, every beat has a door) — but nothing presses the one `use` key at them,
# and there is no picture of any of them. Task #59.
#
# Adding one is not free: `at cast:NAME` FAILS the tour when that person is not
# cast, and who is cast depends on which landscapes the seed dealt to which body.
# Measured on seed 1 at 1024, fifteen of the seventeen were cast and the sulphur
# jungle and the crags were not. So measure the seed before writing the step.
coast calm
wait 0.6

# --- Pell, a clerk in the city where the plan worked -------------------------------------
# Long enough for the street to fill: a villager is built one an even frame, and a
# city that still runs has thirty of them (unspent-ortho-cb).
at cast:pell
wait 2.5
press use
await talking 3
wait 0.4
shot 01-pell-files-him with talking,cast:pell
press pause
wait 0.5
await met:pell 2

# --- Mica, raking behind the machines' rakes on the salt ---------------------------------
at cast:mica
wait 0.8
press use
await talking 3
wait 0.4
shot 02-mica-on-the-salt with talking,cast:mica
press pause
wait 0.5

# --- Brannoc, who listens to the wires over the snow -------------------------------------
at cast:brannoc
wait 0.8
press use
await talking 3
wait 0.4
shot 03-brannoc-on-the-wires with talking,cast:brannoc
press pause
wait 0.5
await met:brannoc 2
